tass 3.0 for OS-9/68000 -- how this tree was built==================================================This is Rich Skrenta's tass 3.0 as adapted to OS-9 and MNews by UlrichDessauer, posted to de.comp.sources.os9 and comp.os.os9 on 1992-12-24("Tass for OS-9", parts 00-03, submitted by Ulrich Dessauer, approved byFrank Kaefer).  The same files, with tabs expanded to spaces and nothingelse different, are TELECOM/tass.lzh (1993-01-24) in the Microware OS-9archive.  ORIG/ holds the posting exactly as extracted.WHAT IT IS FOR.  This port reads the spool of MNews "pre 2" -- Dessauer'snews system as released in January 1993 -- and nothing else.  It reads:  - the active file, <group> <last> <first> <flags>, one group per line    (pre-2's INEWS/wact.c: "%s %08d %08d %c%c");  - the file named by the SysInfo string MNEWS.LIB, plus "/Active"    (default /h0/USR/LIB/NEWS/Active);  - articles under the directory named by the SysInfo string MNEWS.DIR    (default /h0/SPOOL/NEWS), one numbered file each, group dots made    into directories; a file beginning "%(#)$ " is MNews's link to a    cross-posted article and is followed.The 1990 MNews prerelease that CMDS/MNEWS carries writes a different activefile, <group>:<low> <high> <flag>, and names its directories NEWS.DIR andNEWS.LIB, so tass does not read that spool.CHANGES FROM ORIG/ -- one:  mail.c   `typedef long off_t;' under #ifdef OSK is wrapped in the guard           _OSK_COMPAT_OFF_T.  The build uses SRC/COMPAT, whose <types.h>           also supplies off_t under the same guard, and two typedefs of           one name stop the compiler.  Whichever header comes first now           defines it.HOW IT IS BUILT (tools/rebuild/recipes.psv):  tass|tass|curses.c art.c group.c mail.c main.c misc.c page.c prompt.c      screen.c select.c time.c sigs.c|REGEXP APPEND_SIG MNEWS INCSTR      LOCK_INDEX RAND_SIG MEM=20k|/dd/LIB/8bit.l /dd/LIB/termlib.l      /dd/LIB/os9lib.l|-V=../mnews/NN_OSK  The defines are the posting's own Makefile's, and MEM=20k is its -m=20.  <regexp.h> is Henry Spencer's, as carried in SRC/mnews/NN_OSK; regcomp  and regexec come from os9lib.l.  8bit.l is MNews pre-2's character-set  library, built from SRC/mnewspre2/8BIT:  8bit.l|mnewspre2/8BIT|inp.c conv.c c8type.c|NOCOMPAT||-V=/dd/DEFS/os9lib  tass calls only setup_convtable() and conv_charset() from it, and they  do nothing unless CHARSET names a table in /h0/USR/LIB/CHARSET (or the  directory in the SysInfo string CHARSET.LIB).  The Makefile's own target, /h0/ETC/CMDS/tass, is left as posted.The module is trap-free: it runs with cio, csl, math, math881 and csl020all withheld (measured 2026-09-24).